r": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01LcHwGkjaXNcQFFozEyvzpz", "kind": "error", "is_error": true}, {"t_ms": 11287, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01FSpCZm5n9qjfxXhCmVcPsU", "tool": "get_service_status", "args": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 11587, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01FSpCZm5n9qjfxXhCmVcPsU", "tool": "get_service_status", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 11587, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01FSpCZm5n9qjfxXhCmVcPsU", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 14348, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_018t8H3oGMBWLDTb7r4WRt4L", "tool": "rollback", "args": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 18348, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_018t8H3oGMBWLDTb7r4WRt4L", "tool": "rollback", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 18348, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_018t8H3oGMBWLDTb7r4WRt4L", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 20556, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_0172kEa3PEYdV1tbK3tD8TSG", "tool": "get_service_status", "args": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 20856, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_0172kEa3PEYdV1tbK3tD8TSG", "tool": "get_service_status", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 20856, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_0172kEa3PEYdV1tbK3tD8TSG", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 20856, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01UpU2YzhTFx3BWcftyosPjS", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 21156, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01UpU2YzhTFx3BWcftyosPjS", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 21156, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01UpU2YzhTFx3BWcftyosPjS", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 25739, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01Rg46aygGcjJB7NfQq515VN", "tool": "create_incident", "args": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks \u2013 rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "After the v2.3.1 release, checkout-api failed health checks in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), with an error rate of about 18%. Note: v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy in staging. Action taken: rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. The first rollback attempt stopped with an orchestrator error after us-east (partial failure: us-east was on v2.3.0, us-west and eu-west were still on v2.3.1). A retry finished the rollout. Current state: all regions are on v2.3.0, the service is healthy, and the error rate is about 0.2%. Follow-up: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure, find out why v2.3.1 was promoted despite the unhealthy staging RC, and look into the orchestrator error that stopped the rollback."}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 56339, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01Rg46aygGcjJB7NfQq515VN", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTION_UNKNOWN", "error_kind": "timeout", "error_message": "Request to create_incident timed out after 30000ms", "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": "execution", "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 56339, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01Rg46aygGcjJB7NfQq515VN", "kind": "error", "is_error": true}, {"t_ms": 58491, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01Pkomb5QwggTNjVbdbT4tW1", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 58791, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01Pkomb5QwggTNjVbdbT4tW1", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 58791, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01Pkomb5QwggTNjVbdbT4tW1", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 63804, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "checkout-api is back on v2.3.0 in all regions and healthy again, and the SEV2 incident is open as **INC-0001**.\n\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production. v2.3.1 is the broken release, and its release candidate (v2.3.1-rc) also failed health checks in staging.\n  - The first rollback attempt stopped with an orchestrator error after us-east. us-west and eu-west were left on v2.3.1.\n  - I retried once and it finished. us-east, us-west and eu-west are all on v2.3.0, and the error rate has dropped from about 18% to about 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** The request to create the incident timed out. Before trying again, I checked the incident list and found it had been created. I didn't resubmit, so on-call wasn't paged twice. The incident covers the impact, the rollback, the partial failure and retry, and three follow-ups: why v2.3.1 failed, why it was promoted when its staging release candidate was unhealthy, and the orchestrator error that stopped the first rollback.\n\nNo change-manager approval was needed, because v2.3.0 had already been healthy in production.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01Ui3jeMMfNusPLEyLmFM7YB", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_016XiGVmMojcACrJNBT43o57", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "Most recent healthy production release is v2.3.0.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01LcHwGkjaXNcQFFozEyvzpz", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01FSpCZm5n9qjfxXhCmVcPsU", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The rollback stopped partway. Only us-east is on v2.3.0. I'll retry once, since rolling back to the same version is safe to repeat.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_018t8H3oGMBWLDTb7r4WRt4L", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_0172kEa3PEYdV1tbK3tD8TSG", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01UpU2YzhTFx3BWcftyosPjS", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01Rg46aygGcjJB7NfQq515VN", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks \u2013 rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "After the v2.3.1 release, checkout-api failed health checks in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), with an error rate of about 18%. Note: v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy in staging. Action taken: rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. The first rollback attempt stopped with an orchestrator error after us-east (partial failure: us-east was on v2.3.0, us-west and eu-west were still on v2.3.1). A retry finished the rollout. Current state: all regions are on v2.3.0, the service is healthy, and the error rate is about 0.2%. Follow-up: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure, find out why v2.3.1 was promoted despite the unhealthy staging RC, and look into the orchestrator error that stopped the rollback."}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The request timed out, so I'll check whether the incident was created before retrying. That way I don't page on-call twice.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01Pkomb5QwggTNjVbdbT4tW1", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "checkout-api is back on v2.3.0 in all regions and healthy again, and the SEV2 incident is open as **INC-0001**.\n\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production. v2.3.1 is the broken release, and its release candidate (v2.3.1-rc) also failed health checks in staging.\n  - The first rollback attempt stopped with an orchestrator error after us-east. us-west and eu-west were left on v2.3.1.\n  - I retried once and it finished. us-east, us-west and eu-west are all on v2.3.0, and the error rate has dropped from about 18% to about 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** The request to create the incident timed out. Before trying again, I checked the incident list and found it had been created. I didn't resubmit, so on-call wasn't paged twice. The incident covers the impact, the rollback, the partial failure and retry, and three follow-ups: why v2.3.1 failed, why it was promoted when its staging release candidate was unhealthy, and the orchestrator error that stopped the first rollback.\n\nNo change-manager approval was needed, because v2.3.0 had already been healthy in production.", "type": "text"}]}]}